  "releaseNotes": "v1.2.2: type-inference correctness release. Fixed generic-identity conflation in user functions with multiple independent type params (f(a,b)={p=a[0],q=b[0]} now infers {p:Real;q:Char} instead of {p:Any;q:Any}; also removes a silent Int32→Real coercion). Integer division `//` now respects the overflow dialect: MIN // -1 throws under Checked (default) and wraps under Unchecked at every width; `%` never overflows (MIN % -1 = 0 consistently). Fun-argument variance corrected in constraint propagation. Several type-solver soundness fixes (F-bound field checking depth, canonical optional forms) and a large internal hardening pass: ~200 new algebra-law and regression tests.",
